### GET /me/posts - Acceptance Tests
### Test endpoint for getting current user's posts with pagination

@baseUrl = http://localhost/api
@user1Phone = +886901234501
@user1Pass = Pass1234
@user2Phone = +886901234502
@user2Pass = Pass2234

### Step 1: Login as User1
# @name loginUser1
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "{{user1Phone}}",
  "password": "{{user1Pass}}"
}

### Capture user1 token
@user1Token = {{loginUser1.response.body.accessToken}}

### Step 2: Login as User2
# @name loginUser2
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "{{user2Phone}}",
  "password": "{{user2Pass}}"
}

### Capture user2 token
@user2Token = {{loginUser2.response.body.accessToken}}

### Step 3: User1 creates multiple posts
# @name createUser1Post1
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

{
  "content": "User1's first post"
}

###
# @name createUser1Post2
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

{
  "content": "User1's second post",
  "image": "https://example.com/image2.jpg"
}

###
# @name createUser1Post3
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

{
  "content": "User1's third post"
}

### Step 4: User2 creates a post
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user2Token}}

{
  "content": "User2's post"
}

### Test 1: Get all posts for User1 (should only show User1's posts)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

### Expected: 200 OK with { items: [...], total: 3 }
### Should contain only User1's posts, not User2's

---

### Test 2: Get User1's posts with pagination (limit)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/posts?limit=2
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

### Expected: 200 OK with max 2 posts
### Should return: { items: [...], total: 3 }

---

### Test 3: Get User1's posts with pagination (offset)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/posts?limit=2&offset=1
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

### Expected: 200 OK, skips first post
### Should return: { items: [...], total: 3 }

---

### Test 4: Get User1's posts sorted oldest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/posts?sort=oldest
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

### Expected: 200 OK, posts sorted by created_at ASC

---

### Test 5: Get User1's posts sorted newest first (default)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/posts?sort=newest
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

### Expected: 200 OK, posts sorted by created_at DESC

---

### Test 6: Get User2's posts (should only show User2's posts)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{user2Token}}

### Expected: 200 OK with { items: [...], total: 1 }
### Should contain only User2's post

---

### Test 7: Try to access /me/posts without authentication (should get 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/posts

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

---

### Test 8: Invalid limit (too high)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/posts?limit=200
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

### Expected: 400 BAD_REQUEST
### Should return: { errorCode: "BAD_REQUEST", message: "Limit must be between 1 and 100" }

---

### Test 9: Invalid limit (negative)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/posts?limit=-1
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

### Expected: 400 BAD_REQUEST

---

### Test 10: Invalid offset (negative)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/posts?offset=-1
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

### Expected: 400 BAD_REQUEST
### Should return: { errorCode: "BAD_REQUEST", message: "Offset must be >= 0" }

---

### Test 11: Invalid sort value
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/posts?sort=wat
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

### Expected: 400 BAD_REQUEST

---

### Test 12: Verify pagination with limit and offset
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/posts?limit=1&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

### Expected: First post (newest)

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/posts?limit=1&offset=1
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

### Expected: Second post

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/posts?limit=1&offset=2
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

### Expected: Third post (oldest)

---

## Notes
- All /me/posts endpoints REQUIRE authentication
- Same pagination parameters as GET /posts: limit (1-100, default: 20), offset (default: 0)
- Same sort options as GET /posts: "newest" (default) or "oldest"
- Returns PostListResponse with { items: [...], total: N }
- Automatically filters to only show authenticated user's posts
